{"shortDescription":"Management reportPro Kapital delivered a resilient performance during the first nine months of 2026, remaining profitable, maintaining a stable gross profit margin of 35% and strengthening its financial position. The Group continued to advance its residential developments across all three Baltic ca…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Management report"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Pro Kapital delivered a resilient performance during the first nine months of 2026, remaining profitable, maintaining a stable gross profit margin of 35% and strengthening its financial position. The Group continued to advance its residential developments across all three Baltic capitals, supported by its diversified portfolio and disciplined approach to project execution."]},{"type":"p","children":["The year began with improving sentiment in the Baltic real estate market, although geopolitical uncertainty and inflationary pressures subsequently affected buyer confidence. In Tallinn, residential projects in Kristiine City performed broadly in line with expectations, while the Group's premium developments in Vilnius achieved strong market positioning. In Riga, construction progressed at Blue Marine Residence."]},{"type":"p","children":["A major highlight of the reporting period was the highly successful public bond offering in September 2026, demonstrating strong investor confidence in Pro Kapital. The offering was twice oversubscribed, attracting 985 investors across all three Baltic countries and subscriptions totalling EUR 12.0 million. In response to the strong demand, the Group increased the issue size to the maximum of EUR 10 million. The new unsecured bonds carry a fixed annual interest rate of 8.3%, payable quarterly, and mature on 25 September 2028."]},{"type":"p","children":["The proceeds were used for the full early redemption of the Group's senior secured bonds in October 2026. Together with the extension of its existing unsecured bonds, this means that all outstanding bonds now mature in the second half of 2028, providing greater predictability in the Group's financing structure."]},{"type":"p","children":["These achievements reinforce our confidence in the direction we have chosen. We will continue to focus on delivering high-quality developments, completing ongoing projects and carefully timing new investments according to demand in each market. Our priority is not growth for its own sake, but delivering on our commitments to customers and investors."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Key financials"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["The Group remained profitable in the first nine months of 2026, with revenue of EUR 31.7 million (9M 2025: EUR 34.3 million) and net profit of EUR 2.0 million (9M 2025: EUR 6.0 million). Gross margin held steady at 35%."]},{"type":"p","children":["The lower result was partly attributable to a decrease in real estate sales volumes (from 5 000 m² in the first nine months of 2025 to 4 484 m² in the corresponding period of 2026), higher marketing and administrative expenses and a one-off revaluation gain that supported the comparative period. Net profit was further affected by income tax on the Group’s profitable development in Lithuania."]},{"type":"p","children":["Third-quarter revenue was broadly unchanged at EUR 5.6 million (Q3 2025: EUR 5.7 million). However, slightly lower sales volumes and a shift in the sales mix towards lower-margin projects reduced the gross margin to 25% (Q3 2025: 30%). The quarter closed with an operating loss of EUR 0.8 million (Q3 2025: operating profit of EUR 0.2 million) and a net loss of EUR 1.3 million (Q3 2025: net loss of EUR 0.2 million)."]},{"type":"p","children":["Cash generated from operating activities in the first nine months amounted to EUR 5.4 million (9M 2025: EUR 6.8 million), while EUR 3.9 million was used in the third quarter of 2026, reflecting ongoing construction investment."]},{"type":"p","children":["Net asset value per share increased by 15% year-on-year, reaching EUR 1.15 as at 30 September 2026, compared to EUR 1.00 a year earlier, reflecting the continued strengthening of the Group's equity position."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Key performance indicators"]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["in thousands of euros"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["2026 9M"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["2025 9M"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["2026 Q3"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["2025 Q3"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["2025 12M"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Revenue"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["31 684"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["34 265"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["5 597"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["5 746"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["53 162"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Gross profit"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["10 941"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["11 934"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["1 380"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["1 701"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["18 795"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Gross profit, %"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["35%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["35%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["25%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["30%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["35%"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"typ