["Return on equity, % "]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["3.6%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["11.7%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["21.6%"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Return on assets, % "]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["1.8%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["5.1%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["9.9%"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["LTV*, %"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["53.6%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["45.6%"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["45.3%"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Net debt to equity"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["0.57"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["0.73"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["0.63"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Current ratio"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["3.62"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["4.08"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["1.56"]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Net asset value per share, EUR "]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["1.15"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["1.00"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["1.11"]}]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["*LTV as at 30 September 2026 is temporarily elevated due to the timing of the bond refinancing. As at that date, the balance sheet includes both the new unsecured bonds (ISIN EE0000005130) in the amount of EUR 10 million, issued on 25 September 2026, and the senior secured bonds 2020/2028 (ISIN SE0013801172) in the amount of EUR 10.5 million, which were refinanced by the new issue and redeemed in full on 19 October 2026, i.e. after the reporting date."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"i","children":["Equity ratio = equity (owners’ share)/ total assets"]},{"type":"i","children":["Return on equity = net profit (owners’ share) / average equity (owners’ share)"]},{"type":"i","children":["Return on assets = net profit (owners’ share) / average total assets"]},{"type":"i","children":["LTV = total debt / value of real estate assets (inventories and investment property)"]},{"type":"i","children":["Net debt to equity ratio = current and non-current debt less cash/ equity (owners’ share)"]},{"type":"i","children":["Current ratio = current assets / current liabilities"]},{"type":"i","children":["Net asset value per share = equity (owners’ share) / number of shares"]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Real Estate Development"]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Tallinn"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Pro Kapital continued to make strong progress across its Tallinn residential developments during the first nine months of 2026. Sales in Kristiine City remained broadly in line with expectations, supported by demand for well-located, high-quality homes, while construction advanced across several projects. With completed developments generating ongoing sales and a substantial pipeline of new residential properties, the Group remains well positioned for continued development in the Estonian capital."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Kristiine City, the Uus-Kindrali development made solid progress in both sales and construction. As at the date of publication of this report, 93.5% of the total apartments in the white building (Talli 3 / Sammu 8) had been sold, with 6 apartments still available for sale."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, construction of the adjacent seven-storey black building at Sammu 10/Seebi 24a, comprising 90 apartments, was nearing completion. During September, final inspections were carried out with the subcontractors to be ready for client inspections in October. As of the publication date of this report, client inspections are in full swing, the first real rights agreements have been signed and units have been delivered to clients. By the date of publication, 55.6% of the total apartments had been sold."]},{"type":"p","children":["Sales and construction also continued at Musketäri Majad, a development launched in the first quarter of 2026. Located at Sammu 7, Talli 1 and Rivi 8, the project comprises two six- and seven-storey buildings with a total of 144 apartments. By the end of the third quarter, Sammu 7 had reached its full height and Talli 1 had 4 of its 7 floors completed. At Rivi 8, most of the underground concrete works have been completed."]},{"type":"p","children":["Looking ahead, the Group continues preparations for its Dunte development at Tondi Street 53, for which a building permit has already been obtained. The start of construction will be determined in line with market conditions and the Group's development strategy."]},{"type":"p","children":["The remaining projects in the Kristiine City development portfolio are in the active design stage. The building permits for NÜÜD Houses (Marsi 1 / Sõjakooli 13 and Sammu 2/4 / Sõjakooli 15) have been issued, subject to certain conditions agreed with the city, including the developer's obligation to construct and transfer public infrastructure, such as pedestrian sidewalks, to the municipality. In total, these developments are expected to add approximately 43 000 square metres of above- and below-ground gross building area and around 360 units. Approximately 95% of these units would be residential and 5% commercial. This pipeline provides significant opportunities for future growth while allowing the Group to align new investments with market demand."]},{"type":"p","children":["In the Kalaranna District, construction has been completed and sales continue. As at the publication date, 89% of the development's 385 apartments had been sold, with 43 remaining available. The project reinforces Pro Kapital's position in Tallinn's premium residential segment, offering distinctive architecture and a prime waterfront location."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Riga"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["In Riga, Pro Kapital continued to make progress with its Blue Marine Residence development in Klīversala Bay, with construction advancing above ground level during the third quarter. Sales and marketing activities continued alongside the development of the broader Klīversala Bay brand, supporting the project's market positioning and the Group's long-term ambitions in Riga."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Vilnius"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["In Vilnius, the Group maintained sales momentum at the Attico and City Villas developments and continued notary sales."]},{"type":"p","children":["In September, the Group officially completed and unveiled City Villas, its premium residential development in Vilnius Old Town, representing an investment of more than EUR 21 million. Located at the intersection of Šaltinių and Aguonų streets, the completed development comprises four four-storey residential villas and the Attico Boutique commercial building. City Villas marks the architectural highlight of an area developed by Pro Kapital over more than a decade, distinguished by its unique architecture, spacious residences and elevated position overlooking the historic rooftops of Vilnius Old Town."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Group also advanced its newest premium development, Borgo, located in Vilnius Old Town adjacent to the MO Museum. Construction works commenced during the third quarter, marking an important milestone in the project’s development."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Hotel operations"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Third-quarter performance was broadly in line with last year, despite softer demand in July compared with both the previous year and the budget. This was offset by a record-breaking September, with average occupancy reaching 90%, the highest ever recorded by the hotel."]},{"type":"p","children":["The outlook for the fourth quarter remains positive in the individual segment, which is ahead of the same period last year, although MICE demand remains softer."]},{"type":"p","children":["Year-to-date profitability is above last year but still below budget, which nevertheless remains within reach."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Conclusion"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Looking ahead, our priority is to complete ongoing developments, deliver homes to buyers and maintain sales momentum across our Baltic markets. At the same time, we have a substantial pipeline of future projects, giving us the flexibility to decide when to launch new developments based on demand in each market."]},{"type":"p","children":["We believe that success in the current market depends not on how quickly a developer expands, but on how consistently it delivers. For Pro Kapital, this means keeping our commitments to customers, maintaining high standards and making investment decisions that support the company's long-term financial strength."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["CONSOLIDATED INTERIM FINANCIAL STATEMENTS"]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Consolidated interim statements of financial position"]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":2},"children":["in thousands of euros"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["30.09.2026"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["30.09.2025"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["31.12.2025"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":2},"children":[{"type":"b","children":["ASSETS"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[" "]},{"type":"table-data-cel